+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2000-15-1","statement_correct":false,"quote_supports":false,"is_ratio":false,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The court said this plaint gave full details; it did not lay down a rule that a plaintiff must give full details of respondents' conduct in every lawsuit."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2000-15-2","statement_correct":false,"quote_supports":false,"is_ratio":false,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The quoted passage records the pleaded cause of action in this plaint, not an independent legal rule that such a cause of action may generally arise."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2000-15-3","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The court did decide there was one cause of action, but only because the deed-invalidation relief was consequential to the declaration of title and possession claim."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2000-19-1","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":true,"statute_correct":true,"usable":true,"reason":"The judgment directly held that section 760A does not prescribe the mode of application and accepted an affidavit-only substitution application."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2000-20-1","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":true,"statute_correct":true,"usable":true,"reason":"The court held that the original plaint should have been rejected under sections 46(2)(a) and 41 because the encroached portion was not sufficiently described."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2000-20-2","statement_correct":false,"quote_supports":false,"is_ratio":false,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The statement is an overbroad abstraction from the citation to sections 46 and 41 rather than a rule actually decided by the court."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2000-20-3","statement_correct":false,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The court required section 93 notice where an amended plaint was filed after a plan was prepared during an ex parte trial, a material condition missing from the statement."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2000-24-1","statement_correct":false,"quote_supports":false,"is_ratio":false,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The consent of residents was part of the factual background, not a holding that written resident consent is legally required for roadway changes."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2000-24-2","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The court treated R2 and X1C as non-notarial documents affecting land, but the statement omits that their validity was contestable under the Prevention of Frauds and Urban Councils Ordinance context."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2000-24-3","statement_correct":false,"quote_supports":false,"is_ratio":false,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The judgment held the opposite practical point: the dispute concerned all signatories and adjoining owners, so their presence was necessary."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2000-28-1","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":false,"qualifications_ok":true,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The difference between the surveyor's report and oral evidence was a case-specific evidentiary finding, not the ratio as a legal rule."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2000-28-2","statement_correct":false,"quote_supports":false,"is_ratio":false,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The court relied on a material omission in this surveyor's report; it did not state a general duty that every surveyor's report must include all relevant facts."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2000-28-3","statement_correct":false,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The standard of proof holding was limited to contempt proceedings, while the statement incorrectly generalizes it to any case."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2000-3-1","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The court recognized the prior transfer of the fiduciary life interest, but the statement omits the Abolition of Fideicommissa and Entails Act and life-interest context."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2000-3-2","statement_correct":false,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The court dealt with Bibsie's specific transfer of a life interest, not a general proposition that execution of any deed transfers the original entitlement to third parties."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2000-3-3","statement_correct":false,"quote_supports":false,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The judgment vested title in ultimate transferees of the life interest, whereas the statement says transferors and is materially inaccurate."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2000-33-1","statement_correct":false,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":false,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The quote supports a factual finding that the company had not commenced business, but the statement recasts it as a vague evidentiary rule."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2000-33-2","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The court treated continuation rather than winding up as a mixed question of fact and law, but the statement omits the winding-up discretion and burden context."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2000-33-3","statement_correct":false,"quote_supports":false,"is_ratio":false,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The court only said there was no point first agitating in the domestic forum because the 73 percent majority opposed winding up, not that a winding-up order should not be sought."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2000-39-1","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":true,"statute_correct":true,"usable":true,"reason":"The judgment directly held that an executor is not functus officio until the administration of the estate is duly completed."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2000-39-2","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":true,"statute_correct":true,"usable":true,"reason":"The court held that even a reprehensible 33-month delay did not justify reversal without demonstrated prejudice or failure of justice."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2000-39-3","statement_correct":false,"quote_supports":false,"is_ratio":false,"qualifications_ok":false,"statute_correct":true,"usable":false,"reason":"The judgment treated the will reference as an acknowledgment of Lot 11's existence, not as a legal admission of the testator's rights to the property."}
+{"rule_id":"draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2000-45-1","statement_correct":true,"quote_supports":true,"is_ratio":true,"qualifications_ok":true,"statute_correct":true,"usable":true,"reason":"The court applied the rule that contractual intention governs the object of the obligations when deciding whether specific performance was available."}

